Description: wayland: Send synthesized release to press window
 When a drag starts, wl_pointer.leave clears the pointer focus and
 button state. At the end of the drag, releaseButtons() sends a
 synthesized release without a target window. The event can therefore
 reach a different window, while the item that handled the press does
 not receive the release and keeps its drag state active.
 .
 Remember the window that receives the first button press after mouse
 grab routing, and use it as the target of the synthesized release.
 Clear the saved window after the final regular button release.
